  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding Water, Sanitation and Hygiene</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zambia):  The Expanding Water and Sanitation activity facilitates the provision of reliable and sustainable Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services to improve household economic and health outcomes and thereby contribute to rural poverty reduction. The project will improve delivery, promote financially sustainable models for construction, operation and maintenance of WASH services. Further, the project will support the regulatory and institutional capacity of government, civil society and private service providers in WASH planning and budgeting as well as in managing, regulating, and monitoring service delivery. Furthermore, the project will train enterprises to provide WASH services such as household latrine construction and operation and maintenance of water facilities. With FY 2022 funds, USAID will support sustainable WASH service delivery, facilitate private sector participation, improve operation and maintenance, promote good governance and accountability to contribute to water and sanitation service provision, and address policy barriers to improved access to WASH services, promoting financially sustainable, climate-smart models for construction, operation and maintenance of WASH services. This will ultimately contribute to achieving the goal of sustainably improving access to safe drinking water and sanitation services by addressing both the water supply and demand side constraints while also addressing the business enabling environment for provision of WASH services. Under USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy, the mechanism will support Development Objective 3: Capacity of Zambia&apos;s Government, Citizens and Private Sector to Improve Health and Economic Outcomes and Meet Critical Needs of Vulnerable Populations. More broadly, this mechanism contributes to the U.S. foreign policy priority of working with partner countries to accelerate water security and advance resilience, prosperity, and stability.... ..</narrative>
  </description>
